that you would've gotten recognized a lot

01:22:27.187 --> 01:22:29.498
or it would've been like
a daily occurrence, so-

01:22:29.498 --> 01:22:32.006
- Yeah, I think initially
when I moved it probably was,

01:22:32.006 --> 01:22:33.846
but then now people know you're there.

01:22:33.846 --> 01:22:34.679
They kind of just-

01:22:34.679 --> 01:22:35.512
- Right.
- Like there's

01:22:35.512 --> 01:22:36.806
no sense of urgency, right.

01:22:36.806 --> 01:22:37.905
- Right, right, right, right.

01:22:37.905 --> 01:22:40.086
- Some people still have
to like you look familiar,

01:22:40.086 --> 01:22:41.767
but then they don't really
go any further than that.

01:22:41.767 --> 01:22:42.600
(laughing)

01:22:42.600 --> 01:22:44.977
Yeah, I guess like different
sensibility as well.

01:22:44.977 --> 01:22:46.948
- We were saying you
were a versus America.

01:22:46.948 --> 01:22:47.781
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:22:47.781 --> 01:22:49.577
- People here aren't as starstruck.

01:22:49.577 --> 01:22:50.410
Yeah.

01:22:50.410 --> 01:22:51.243
- I don't think so.

01:22:51.243 --> 01:22:52.216
You guys, Brighton's a cool city.

01:22:52.216 --> 01:22:53.086
Come visit Brighton.

01:22:53.086 --> 01:22:54.108
It's amazing city.

01:22:54.108 --> 01:22:55.266
- No don't, you'll ruin it.

01:22:55.266 --> 01:22:56.514
(laughing)

01:22:56.514 --> 01:22:58.265
It's nice, I like it.

01:22:58.265 --> 01:23:00.466
- Don't make it to VidCon.

01:23:00.466 --> 01:23:01.299
Yeah.

01:23:01.299 --> 01:23:03.115
- We thought about that
for a while as well.

01:23:03.115 --> 01:23:04.764
Like maybe we'll move to L.A. still

01:23:04.764 --> 01:23:06.375
and Brighton's just nice.

01:23:06.375 --> 01:23:07.208
- Right.
- Every time we come back,

01:23:07.208 --> 01:23:09.245
it's like, man, we have a nice house.

01:23:09.245 --> 01:23:10.188
We live in a nice part of town.

01:23:10.188 --> 01:23:11.021
The people are cool.

01:23:11.021 --> 01:23:12.075
The restaurants are really nice.

01:23:12.075 --> 01:23:14.923
- Yeah, like L.A. just
seems intense, you know,

01:23:14.923 --> 01:23:16.756
from my experience with it.

01:23:16.756 --> 01:23:17.856
- It's too city, I feel.

01:23:17.856 --> 01:23:20.994
And especially the culture behind it

01:23:20.994 --> 01:23:24.195
is definitely, you know,
I feel run by this like,

01:23:24.195 --> 01:23:25.620
you know, stardom culture.

01:23:25.620 --> 01:23:26.770
- So it's (indistinct)

01:23:26.770 --> 01:23:28.236
- Yeah, exactly, exactly.

01:23:28.236 --> 01:23:30.185
- Doesn't really 'cause
I said it before that,

01:23:30.185 --> 01:23:31.115
when I went on tour,

01:23:31.115 --> 01:23:32.827
you get a good sense of like life

01:23:32.827 --> 01:23:34.067
in different pockets of the world.

01:23:34.067 --> 01:23:34.900
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:23:34.900 --> 01:23:36.634
- And then like going around
different states, I was like,

01:23:36.634 --> 01:23:38.417
oh this is kind of like that state,

01:23:38.417 --> 01:23:39.275
but you guys do this instead

01:23:39.275 --> 01:23:41.285
and you kinda get a feel
for the culture a bit.

01:23:41.285 --> 01:23:43.668
Everything still felt like
quintessentially America.

01:23:43.668 --> 01:23:44.574
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah.

01:23:44.574 --> 01:23:47.245
- But then L.A.is just a different beast.

01:23:47.245 --> 01:23:50.295
It feels like we would go down the streets

01:23:50.295 --> 01:23:52.391
and like walk around and you
can get a sense for the place,

01:23:52.391 --> 01:23:54.033
like who's walking around
and who lives there,

01:23:54.033 --> 01:23:55.918
and like they're just a slice of life.

01:23:55.918 --> 01:23:56.916
- Yeah.
- But LA is so hard

01:23:56.916 --> 01:23:58.356
to find that with.

01:23:58.356 --> 01:24:00.556
Anywhere you walk in it,
which is very few places.

01:24:00.556 --> 01:24:02.654
It feels like everyone's
just there to work,

01:24:02.654 --> 01:24:04.774
even no one lives there.

01:24:04.774 --> 01:24:07.876
- Yeah, like every time I
meet like someone in L.A.,

01:24:07.876 --> 01:24:10.076
you just get used to people
introducing themselves,

01:24:10.076 --> 01:24:12.276
then saying what they do immediately.

01:24:12.276 --> 01:24:13.109
- Right.
- You know, normally

01:24:13.109 --> 01:24:15.600
that's like a few layers
down in the conversation,

01:24:15.600 --> 01:24:18.247
but in L.A., it feels like,
okay, I'm this person,

01:24:18.247 --> 01:24:19.895
by the way, I also do this.

01:24:19.895 --> 01:24:20.975
I'm working on this, this, this.

01:24:20.975 --> 01:24:21.955
And that's just like,

01:24:21.955 --> 01:24:22.936
that was just like

01:24:22.936 --> 01:24:24.204
very forward for me.
- Working on screenplay.

01:24:24.204 --> 01:24:25.037
- Sorry?

01:24:25.037 --> 01:24:25.870
- Working on screenplay.

01:24:25.870 --> 01:24:26.703
- Working on screenplay.

01:24:26.703 --> 01:24:28.814
- I got propositioned one in an Uber in LA

01:24:28.814 --> 01:24:30.814
and then on the same trip,

01:24:30.814 --> 01:24:32.562
we heard a guy walking down
the street and it was like,

01:24:32.562 --> 01:24:34.282
I just don't think they're
gonna go for that screenplay.

01:24:34.282 --> 01:24:35.572
Maybe if we pitched on
this other one, I was like,

01:24:35.572 --> 01:24:38.572
no fucken way people talk like this.

01:24:39.515 --> 01:24:41.957
I was like are we in a movie?

01:24:41.957 --> 01:24:43.054
- Walk on set.

01:24:43.054 --> 01:24:44.254
- Yeah.

01:24:44.254 --> 01:24:46.226
You're in like the traffic and
that someone like practicing

01:24:46.226 --> 01:24:48.292
their lines in the car
next to you or something.

01:24:48.292 --> 01:24:49.125
- Yeah, exactly, yeah.

01:24:49.125 --> 01:24:51.111
- Did you hear horror stories
of people who move there

01:24:51.111 --> 01:24:53.093
and then like change and become Hollywood?

01:24:53.093 --> 01:24:54.230
- [Garnt] Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:24:54.230 --> 01:24:55.422
- I think it's impossible not to.

01:24:55.422 --> 01:24:56.688
That was another thing.

01:24:56.688 --> 01:24:58.818
I was kind of afraid to
move there in case I did-

01:24:58.818 --> 01:24:59.976
- Become this monster.

01:24:59.976 --> 01:25:00.809
- Yeah.

01:25:00.809 --> 01:25:01.642
Yeah.

01:25:01.642 --> 01:25:03.225
- 'Cause I'm a sponge, I'll
just take in what's around me.

01:25:03.225 --> 01:25:05.065
And I'm like, if I'm surrounded
by that all the time,

01:25:05.065 --> 01:25:06.096
that's all you know, and-

01:25:06.096 --> 01:25:07.227
- Yeah, yeah.

01:25:07.227 --> 01:25:08.866
It's very disconnected
from the rest of the world.

01:25:08.866 --> 01:25:10.506
If you like, when we come
back here and we live here,

01:25:10.506 --> 01:25:12.476
it's like, people don't talk the same.

01:25:12.476 --> 01:25:13.907
They're not talking about
stocks all the time.

01:25:13.907 --> 01:25:16.558
Like investing in houses and-

01:25:16.558 --> 01:25:17.779
- Scrap the next topic, then-

01:25:17.779 --> 01:25:20.029
(laughing)

01:25:23.897 --> 01:25:26.409
- I think that's like another big reason

01:25:26.409 --> 01:25:28.625
why like I probably could
never see myself living

01:25:28.625 --> 01:25:30.607
in a place like that
'cause it's like, yeah.

01:25:30.607 --> 01:25:32.879
Again, like I don't wanna be that guy.

01:25:32.879 --> 01:25:35.059
- Yeah, yeah.
- Who turns into that, right?

01:25:35.059 --> 01:25:38.017
- Yeah.
- Like, love all the people.

01:25:38.017 --> 01:25:39.540
I love all my friends that live in L.A.

01:25:39.540 --> 01:25:40.373
- For sure.

01:25:40.373 --> 01:25:41.206
- They're all amazing people.

01:25:41.206 --> 01:25:42.039
But you know, at the same time, yeah,

01:25:42.039 --> 01:25:44.637
it is kind of like another world.

01:25:44.637 --> 01:25:45.470
- Yeah.

01:25:45.470 --> 01:25:46.587
- It doesn't feel real.

01:25:46.587 --> 01:25:48.238
- I mean I have so many friends there

01:25:48.238 --> 01:25:50.608
and so many of them just
complain about L.A. all the time.

01:25:50.608 --> 01:25:52.868
Like they don't even want to be there.

01:25:52.868 --> 01:25:55.469
- But they can't leave.
- Yeah, it's hard to get out.

01:25:55.469 --> 01:25:57.625
- Well, it's the best place
for this type of work.

01:25:57.625 --> 01:25:59.420
- It is.
- I'm never more productive

01:25:59.420 --> 01:26:00.590
than when I go to LA.

01:26:00.590 --> 01:26:01.654
- [All] Yeah, it's true.

01:26:01.654 --> 01:26:03.654
- There's always something that
you can be working on from-

01:26:03.654 --> 01:26:04.487
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:26:04.487 --> 01:26:05.343
- Infinite connections, right?

01:26:05.343 --> 01:26:07.323
- Yeah, I feel like if
you want to network,

01:26:07.323 --> 01:26:09.384
then L.A. is the place to be.

01:26:09.384 --> 01:26:10.217
- Yeah.

01:26:10.217 --> 01:26:11.589
- But at what cost?

01:26:11.589 --> 01:26:13.355
- Is there no part of you that ever wanted

01:26:13.355 --> 01:26:15.960
to try living in Korea for a bit?

01:26:15.960 --> 01:26:16.864
- I don't think so.

01:26:16.864 --> 01:26:18.617
I think it's too much of
a culture shift for me.

01:26:18.617 --> 01:26:20.714
- That's right.
- Makes sense.

01:26:20.714 --> 01:26:22.268
And I'm a very social person

01:26:22.268 --> 01:26:24.280
and I feel like I would not integrate

01:26:24.280 --> 01:26:26.050
as much as I would want to.

01:26:26.050 --> 01:26:26.883
- [All] Right.

01:26:26.883 --> 01:26:28.369
- I feel like I would be
very scared and nervous

01:26:28.369 --> 01:26:30.590
to speak Korean to people.

01:26:30.590 --> 01:26:33.188
And I would never go out
and join like a book club

01:26:33.188 --> 01:26:35.570
or go meet people at like an
event or anything like that.

01:26:35.570 --> 01:26:36.403
- Right.
- That's right, right, right.

01:26:36.403 --> 01:26:37.971
- True, true.
- It would be scary.

01:26:37.971 --> 01:26:40.479
- Would you ever, are you planning to,

01:26:40.479 --> 01:26:43.259
I guess like stay in UK and Ireland then?

01:26:43.259 --> 01:26:46.918
Do you see yourself sticking
around this kind of area?

01:26:46.918 --> 01:26:48.809
- I think it's nice enough.

01:26:48.809 --> 01:26:50.468
I think if we've carved out like

01:26:50.468 --> 01:26:53.484
a nice, niche place for us here.

01:26:53.484 --> 01:26:56.995
And I think, again, it
keeps me very like grounded

01:26:56.995 --> 01:26:59.413
and keeps me like very
in touch with the world.

01:26:59.413 --> 01:27:00.246
- Yeah.

01:27:00.246 --> 01:27:02.585
- And like walking around
here and in Brighton,

01:27:02.585 --> 01:27:04.585
I feel like I'm actually like a part

01:27:04.585 --> 01:27:06.834
of like the bigger picture in a weird way.

01:27:06.834 --> 01:27:07.885
- No, that's awesome.

01:27:07.885 --> 01:27:09.853
- It doesn't feel like a
bubble, like everywhere else,

01:27:09.853 --> 01:27:12.674
but I've done LA for like
three months at one point.

01:27:12.674 --> 01:27:14.326
And it was really fun.

01:27:14.326 --> 01:27:16.183
I had a lot of friends
there and like every night

01:27:16.183 --> 01:27:19.094
was to hang out with so many
good restaurants in L.A.

01:27:19.094 --> 01:27:22.705
- Yeah, that is one thing that
every time I go back to L.A.,

01:27:22.705 --> 01:27:25.195
I'm looking forward to
the restaurant and foods.

01:27:25.195 --> 01:27:27.053
- Yeah, it's like the only
place outside of Korea

01:27:27.053 --> 01:27:28.664
that has good Korean barbecue.

01:27:28.664 --> 01:27:29.796
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:27:29.796 --> 01:27:31.141
- Korean barbecue's so good.

01:27:31.141 --> 01:27:32.246
- Korean barbecue is really good.

01:27:32.246 --> 01:27:34.183
- I'm so excited for that like,

01:27:34.183 --> 01:27:37.182
'cause we're going to LA
actually in about two weeks,

01:27:37.182 --> 01:27:38.015
two, three weeks.

01:27:38.015 --> 01:27:38.848
- From recording, yeah.

01:27:38.848 --> 01:27:40.402
- Yeah, yeah, from a
time with this recording

01:27:40.402 --> 01:27:42.213
and the first place I always wanna hit up

01:27:42.213 --> 01:27:44.413
is the Korean barbecue.

01:27:44.413 --> 01:27:46.194
- Of course, then you can
eat meat. It's just insane.

01:27:46.194 --> 01:27:49.405
You get it in Japan, it's
like all you can eat maybe.

01:27:49.405 --> 01:27:51.702
Maybe if you are lucky and wear nice.

01:27:51.702 --> 01:27:53.704
- Well, Korean barbecue,
I feel is very different

01:27:53.704 --> 01:27:55.373
to like Yucky Nicu, right?

01:27:55.373 --> 01:27:57.285
- Yeah, yeah it is.
- Yucky Nicu is really good.

01:27:57.285 --> 01:27:58.914
- It is.
- They are both amazing,

01:27:58.914 --> 01:28:00.756
but it's like it's definitely
a different vibe, I feel.

01:28:00.756 --> 01:28:02.678
- Do you have any favorite Korean dishes

01:28:02.678 --> 01:28:05.996
or just any favorite food in general?

01:28:05.996 --> 01:28:09.026
- I mean I'm a sucker for just
a good piping (indistinct)

01:28:09.026 --> 01:28:10.135
- Oh God.
- Yes.

01:28:10.135 --> 01:28:12.775
- In like the proper Korean
one, like the stone bowl.

01:28:12.775 --> 01:28:13.608
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

01:28:13.608 --> 01:28:15.667
- It's still crackling as it comes out.

01:28:15.667 --> 01:28:16.500
- Yeah.

01:28:16.500 --> 01:28:18.173
It's just really good and
it's nice and spicy and warm

01:28:18.173 --> 01:28:19.405
and it's good winter food,

01:28:19.405 --> 01:28:21.446
but there's also another one called,

01:28:21.446 --> 01:28:22.706
I think it's seolleongtang,

01:28:22.706 --> 01:28:25.425
which is like an ox-bone broth.

01:28:25.425 --> 01:28:28.026
- Yeah, I've had that once and it's-

01:28:28.026 --> 01:28:29.666
- It's very tasty.

01:28:29.666 --> 01:28:32.678
- It's tasty and it just cleans the soul.

01:28:32.678 --> 01:28:33.596
That's what it feels like.

01:28:33.596 --> 01:28:36.997
I remember one time, I was
like one of the most hungover

01:28:36.997 --> 01:28:38.186
I've ever been in Korea.

01:28:38.186 --> 01:28:39.041
- Yeah.
- I felt awful

01:28:39.041 --> 01:28:41.461
and had like the ox-bone soup

01:28:41.461 --> 01:28:43.724
and it just felt like
my body was just like

01:28:43.724 --> 01:28:45.364
so refreshed afterwards.

01:28:45.364 --> 01:28:46.197
- Yeah.

01:28:46.197 --> 01:28:47.564
- I don't know what you guys put in there,

01:28:47.564 --> 01:28:49.724
but like it's like the ancient herbal,

01:28:49.724 --> 01:28:52.070
like the ancient herbal medicine

01:28:52.070 --> 01:28:54.603
that everyone talks about,
that's what it felt like.

01:28:54.603 --> 01:28:55.436
- Used for a thousand.

01:28:55.436 --> 01:28:56.269
- Right.

01:28:56.269 --> 01:28:57.269
- Mix it in.

01:28:58.324 --> 01:28:59.157
- Yeah.

01:28:59.157 --> 01:29:00.962
I'm a big fan of like a Mandu chicken,

01:29:00.962 --> 01:29:02.663
which is like a dumpling stew as well.

01:29:02.663 --> 01:29:03.496
- Okay, okay.

01:29:03.496 --> 01:29:07.232
- It's stuff that I
wouldn't get here really.

01:29:07.232 --> 01:29:09.542
And it was like, yeah, it's so good.

01:29:09.542 --> 01:29:10.375
- There's probably a lot of stuff

01:29:10.375 --> 01:29:12.581
that you can't really get here, right?

01:29:12.581 --> 01:29:13.414
- Yeah.

01:29:13.414 --> 01:29:14.285
- At least not proper.

01:29:14.285 --> 01:29:15.973
- Yeah. I still stand by the Korean food

01:29:15.973 --> 01:29:17.175
is my favorite food in the world.

01:29:17.175 --> 01:29:18.432
- I love Korean fried chicken.

01:29:18.432 --> 01:29:19.265
- I love it.
- It's amazing.

01:29:19.265 --> 01:29:20.700
- Korean fried chicken is
also fucken incredible.

01:29:20.700 --> 01:29:23.621
- I don't realize that Koreans
have perfected fried chicken.

01:29:23.621 --> 01:29:24.844
- It's the best, they have the best.

01:29:24.844 --> 01:29:27.543
- I think Koreans have the best
fried chicken in the world.

01:29:27.543 --> 01:29:29.661
- To be fair, I don't
think I've ever heard

01:29:29.661 --> 01:29:31.314
or met anyone who has said

01:29:31.314 --> 01:29:32.954
that they don't like Korean food, so-

01:29:32.954 --> 01:29:33.787
- Yeah.

01:29:33.787 --> 01:29:34.620
It's pretty difficult.

01:29:34.620 --> 01:29:35.453
- The British haven't
had it, that's a lot-

01:29:35.453 --> 01:29:36.773
- Well, they haven't had the good one.

01:29:36.773 --> 01:29:40.994
- Yeah, because I guess like
Korean food wasn't as popular,

01:29:40.994 --> 01:29:43.472
I guess like 10 years ago or something.

01:29:43.472 --> 01:29:45.582
'Cause I remember like I'd
never even tried Korean food

01:29:45.582 --> 01:29:48.781
until around like 10 years ago.

01:29:48.781 --> 01:29:50.615
And then 'cause it was all like, you know,

01:29:50.615 --> 01:29:53.142
you see like Indian food
or like Japanese food

01:29:53.142 --> 01:29:55.538
or Chinese food and like
I'd never got a chance

01:29:55.538 --> 01:29:57.576
to try Korean cuisine.

01:29:57.576 --> 01:29:58.409
And then remember the
first time trying it.

01:29:58.409 --> 01:30:00.963
I was like, why is this
not more, more popular?

01:30:00.963 --> 01:30:02.893
You know, why is this not more widespread?

01:30:02.893 --> 01:30:03.874
- Yeah.

01:30:03.874 --> 01:30:05.822
K-Pop are doing a lot of the
heavy lifting on that one.

01:30:05.822 --> 01:30:07.942
- Yes, yes, yes, yes.

01:30:07.942 --> 01:30:10.381
- Yeah, spreading into
the world, which is great.

01:30:10.381 --> 01:30:14.182
'Cause now we have like a good
Korean restaurant in Brighton

01:30:14.182 --> 01:30:16.262
called Cogi, which is just meat.

01:30:16.262 --> 01:30:19.109
But it does like legit Korean food.

01:30:19.109 --> 01:30:20.183
- Cool.
- It's so good.

01:30:20.183 --> 01:30:22.415
- Gotta check it out, I think that's new.

01:30:22.415 --> 01:30:25.420
- Is it new since, or has
it been around for a while?

01:30:25.420 --> 01:30:27.503
- I think it was right before pandemic

01:30:27.503 --> 01:30:29.860
and I'm so happy that
pandemic didn't kill it.

01:30:29.860 --> 01:30:30.693
- Okay.

01:30:30.693 --> 01:30:31.804
- Because I was very worried.

01:30:31.804 --> 01:30:33.154
I was like, you haven't
been open long enough

01:30:33.154 --> 01:30:35.100
to like have a float of cash.

01:30:35.100 --> 01:30:36.925
- Yeah, right.
- It's like survive this,

01:30:36.925 --> 01:30:38.684
but I think there's still going strong.

01:30:38.684 --> 01:30:39.894
- Yeah, 'cause I feel like in Brighton now

01:30:39.894 --> 01:30:40.933
there's just like,

01:30:40.933 --> 01:30:43.243
like there's been a lot of
restaurants been popping up now

